      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the test. I'll improve understandability by splitting the single monolithic test into focused, descriptively-named test methods, and by adding concise comments that explain the phonetic reasoning rather than just restating the values.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test splits the original monolithic `testDifference` method into four focused, descriptively-named test methods (`testDifferenceWithNullAndBlankInputs`, `testDifferenceWithVariousNamePairs`, `testDifferenceExamplesFromMsdnDeDz`, `testDifferenceExamplesFromMsdnSetuSus`), each with a brief Javadoc explaining the phonetic reasoning — preserving all original assertions and call signatures exactly."
